---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { MODULES } from '../data/curriculum.js';
import { href } from '../lib/site.js';
---
<Layout url="about.html" title="About" description="Paipa breaks cloud engineering into topics, puts them in the order they build on each other, and covers each one in depth.">
<main class="about">
<h1>About</h1>
<p>Paipa teaches cloud engineering: how to design, build, secure and run systems on the cloud. It breaks the subject into {MODULES.length} topics, puts them in the order they build on each other, and covers each one in depth: Linux and networking first, then the core AWS services, networking and security on AWS, automation, running systems at scale, and designing whole systems.</p>
<p>It uses one cloud provider, AWS, so every example fits together. The ideas carry over to other clouds, under different names.</p>
<p>The name comes from the pipeline: the path every change takes from a commit to production, and the path the roadmap follows.</p>

<h2>How to use it</h2>
<p>Start at the top of the <a href={href('roadmap.html')}>roadmap</a> and work down. Each topic explains why it matters, the core ideas and the commands to run. Some end with a <a href={href('labs.html')}>lab</a> you can do on your own computer.</p>
<p>Notes are added one topic at a time. A topic becomes a link on the roadmap once its notes are ready.</p></main>
</Layout>
